    // Drift: a field starts this many seconds into its drift, so the first frame (and every capture) is already full, and motes rise from this far below the bottom edge. Each mote's own constants are a base plus a random share of a spread: how long one rise takes, how much of the height it climbs, how far and how slowly it sways, and its radius (embers and ash apart). Once the bloom passes a mote's threshold it fades out over this much of the bloom range.
